        <core:definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A process state is a state where a device or service is executing a planned process or is in a specific configuration. [Allotrope]</core:definition>
        <core:note rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The subclasses follow the model of ISA-S88. [Allotrope]</core:note>
        <core:note rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">These classes are mainly used in procedure specifications or conditions. [Allotrope]</core:note>
        <core:prefLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">process state</core:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


