        <core:definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The calibration curve is a data distribution function of the instrumental response, the so-called analytical signal, changed with the concentration of the analyte (the substance to be measured). [Wikipedia]</core:definition>
