        <core:definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Signal-to-noise ratio (USP621) is a signal-to-noise ratio (peak-to-peak) where the noise is calculated over a period that is a minimum of 5 times the peak width. [Allotrope]</core:definition>
        <core:prefLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">signal-to-noise ratio (USP621)</core:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


