        <core:definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">An impedance scan characteristic frequency is an impedance scan result datum obtained from the infliction point of the impedance spectrum that provides an indication of the average cell diameter. The larger the cell diameter, the smaller the fc and vice-versa. [Allotrope]</core:definition>
        <core:prefLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">impedance scan characteristic frequency</core:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


