        <core:definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A specific rotation result is is a quality quantification facet quantifying the change in orientation of monochromatic plane-polarized light, per unit distance–concentration product, as the light passes through a sample of a compound in solution. [Wikipedia]</core:definition>
        <core:prefLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">specific rotation</core:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


