        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A xenobiotic (Greek, xenos &quot;foreign&quot;; bios &quot;life&quot;) is a compound that is foreign to a living organism. Principal xenobiotics include: drugs, carcinogens and various compounds that have been introduced into the environment by artificial means.</obo:IAO_0000115>
